               <head>Kullīyāt-i Rafīʻ</head>
               <msContents class="http://id.loc.gov/authorities/subjects/sh89005046">
                  <summary> Collected poetry (<title>Kullīyāt</title>) by the
                     seventeenth-century poet Mīrzā Ḥasan Bayg Rafīʿ of Mashhad, comprising ghazals,
                     rubāʿīs and short masnavīs. Rafīʿ migrated to India during the reign of
                     Shāhjahān and served as panegyrist to both Shāhjahān and Dārā Shikūh. According
                     to the <title>Makhzan al-gharāʾib</title> (<title>Bodleian Catalogue</title>,
                     Ethé 395, col. 333), he was still living in 1083 (1672–1673). He died in Delhi
                     before 1093 (1682), when Sarkhvush composed his <title>Kalimāt
                        al-shu'arā'</title> (A. Sprenger, <title>Catalogue</title>, p. 111). </summary>
                  <msItem xml:id="Uk_IO_Islamic_471-item1">
                     <author key="">
                        <persName xml:lang="fa-Latn-x-lc">Mīrzā Ḥasan Bayg Rafīʿ</persName>
                        <persName xml:lang="fa">میرزا حسن بیگ رفیع</persName>
                     </author>
                     <title xml:lang="fa-Latn-x-lc" key="">Kullīyāt-i Rafīʿ</title>
                     <title xml:lang="fa">كليات رفيع</title>
                     <incipit xml:lang="fa">(f. 1r) زين نام بهرعنوان ظاهر شده فرمانها...[The first
                        hemistich is damaged] </incipit>
                     <explicit xml:lang="fa">(f. 283v) کسی عقل کل را نسنجد بزر | ندارد قرینی سخن
                        مختصر </explicit>
                     <colophon> The colophon was added in a later hand and gives the date of completion as 8 Ramaẓān, regnal year
                        16, probably of Muḥammad Shāh (12 February 1734). The scribe's name has been
                        cut away in binding. </colophon>
                     <note><p>The <title>Kullīyāt</title> comprises:<list>
                              <item><locus from="1r" to="251r">ff. 1r–251r</locus>Ghazals, arranged
                                 alphabetically. </item>
                              <item><locus from="251r" to="258v">ff. 251r–258v</locus>Rubāʿīs. </item>
                              <item><locus from="258v" to="283r">ff. 258v–283r</locus>Short
                                 masnavīs: <list rend="bulleted">
                                    <item><title>Dar taʿrīf-i Shāhjahān Pādshāh</title> (<locus>f.
                                          258v</locus>)</item>
                                    <item><title>Dar ṣifat-i ʿimārāt</title> (<locus>f.
                                       264r</locus>)</item>
                                    <item><title>Sitāyish-i asp</title> (<locus>f.
                                       266v</locus>)</item>
                                    <item><title>Mazammat-i asp</title> (<locus>f.
                                       268v</locus>)</item>
                                    <item><title>Hajv-i shakhsī</title> (<locus>f.
                                       270v</locus>)</item>
                                    <item><title>Taʿrīf-i Shāhjahān</title> (<locus>f.
                                       272r</locus>)</item>
                                    <item><title>Taʿrīf-i masjid</title> (<locus>f.
                                       276r</locus>)</item>
                                    <item><title>Taʿrīf-i qaṣr</title> (<locus>f.
                                       277v</locus>)</item>
                                    <item><title>Taʿrīf-i burj</title> (<locus>f.
                                       278r</locus>)</item>
                                    <item><title>Taʿrīf-i khāṣṣ va ʿāmm</title> (<locus>f.
                                          279v</locus>)</item>
                                    <item><title>Taʿrīf-i takht-i muraṣṣaʿ</title> (<locus>f.
                                          280r</locus>)</item>
                                    <item><title>Taʿrīf-i ḥammām</title> (<locus>f.
                                       281r</locus>)</item>
                                    <item><title>Taʿrīf-i bāgh</title> (<locus>f.
                                       282v</locus>)</item>
                                    <item><title>Taʿrīf-i ʿĪd-i vazn</title> (<locus>f.
                                       283r</locus>)</item>
                                 </list>
                              </item>
                           </list></p></note>
                     <textLang mainLang="fa">Persian</textLang>
                  </msItem>
               </msContents>

